1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,420
The bomb knows nothing.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:02,860
No computer.

3
00:00:02,890 --> 00:00:03,590
No sensor.

4
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:04,300
No steering.

5
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:05,250
Only physics.

6
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,190
Gravity pulls it down,

7
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:09,270
its speed carries it forward:

8
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:10,460
a ballistic curve.

9
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:13,020
Drag slows it down.

10
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:14,490
Wind pushes it off course.

11
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:16,100
The error is set at release.

12
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,780
So the intelligence must be in the aircraft.

13
00:00:19,810 --> 00:00:20,370
A computer

14
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,300
measures speed,

15
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:21,650
altitude

16
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:22,280
and wind,

17
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:24,380
and solves the trajectory.

18
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,420
The CCIP

19
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:28,310
shows where the bomb would land

20
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:29,500
if released now.

21
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:31,500
The pilot moves the marker

22
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:32,550
onto the target,

23
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:33,440
and releases.

24
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:37,000
The CCRP

25
00:00:37,030 --> 00:00:40,730
reverses the problem: the pilot flies to the target,

26
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:42,380
and the computer calculates

27
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:43,290
the release point.

28
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:44,820
Unguided rockets

29
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:47,110
work the same way: no steering,

30
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:49,060
only a predicted impact point.

31
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,640
But after release,

32
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:52,930
nothing can be corrected.

33
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,140
The impact

34
00:00:55,170 --> 00:00:56,090
is a function

35
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:56,860
of the release.
